13/30 May 1675 (prov. 24 Jun 1675), will, Thomas Salmon of Cecil County, son Peter Salmon - heir Elizabeth Bayley - heir Thomas Howell Jr. - heir John Howell - heir Nathaniel Howell - witn. William Dunkerton + John Dixon
23 Mar 1674/5 (prov. 17 Sep 1675), will, Verlinder Stone of Charles County, son John Stone [given my negro woman] - heir Benoni Thomas - daughter Doyen - witn. Margaret Bagghay + Barberie Kendall
5 Oct 1675 (prov. 28 Nov 1675), will, Capt. Thomas Howell of Cecil County, wife Elizabeth Howell - son John Howell - son Nathaniel Howell - daughter Vanheeke - witn. Robert Sanders + Robert Brooke
9 Feb 1675 (prov. 1 Jul 1676), will, William Morgan in the County of Cecil, wife Martha - son James - witn. George Wharton + William Welsh
23 Feb 1675 (prov. 20 Jun 1676), will, John Morgan late of Cecil County planter, cousin Benjamin Perke - heir John Denning - wife Elizabeth Morgan - witn. John Denning + Ed Williams
2 Mar 1675/6 (prov. 6 Jun 1676), will, John Owen of Cecil County, father John Owen of London Marcht. - heir Thomas Matthews and wife - heir George Eade - heir John James - witn. John Dixon + Mary Mills
